## Testing

- Every Go package with non-exempt code ships meaningful tests of its behavior.
- Exempt only files named `main.go` and files beneath any `cmd/` directory; keep behavior out of them.
- Report the checks you actually ran and their measured results; never claim unexecuted validation passed.

## Style

Follow `.rubric/style.md`. Sources, in precedence order after the overrides below:
[Go Code Review Comments](https://go.dev/wiki/CodeReviewComments),
[Go in production: formatting and style](https://peter.bourgon.org/go-in-production/#formatting-and-style), and
[Uber Go Style Guide](https://github.com/uber-go/guide/blob/master/style.md).

- Do not add explanatory inline or trailing comments in Go code.
- Exported application symbols require documentation comments.
- A declaration's documentation comment has at most two physical lines, each at most 150 Unicode characters including `//`.
